WEBVTT

00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:02.900
Are you a SMART fella,

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.933
or a FART smella?

00:00:04.933 --> 00:00:06.433
Let's find OUT!

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:08.267
Okay,

00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:10.267
a number series!

00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:10.933
Five,

00:00:10.933 --> 00:00:11.567
fourteen,

00:00:11.567 --> 00:00:12.233
twenty-three,

00:00:12.233 --> 00:00:12.900
thirty-two,

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.233
and then...

00:00:14.233 --> 00:00:16.233
what comes next?

00:00:16.233 --> 00:00:16.900
A.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:17.567
Forty,

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:18.200
B.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:18.867
Forty-two,

00:00:18.867 --> 00:00:19.533
C.

00:00:19.533 --> 00:00:20.200
Forty-one,

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.533
or D.

00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:22.200
Fifty?

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.533
Five seconds!

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.500
TIME'S UP!

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:32.933
The answer is...

00:00:32.933 --> 00:00:33.533
C,

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:34.133
forty-one!

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:37.700
Each number goes up by nine:

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:38.300
five,

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:38.900
fourteen,

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:39.500
twenty-three,

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:40.067
thirty-two,

00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:43.633
so thirty-two plus nine is forty-one.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:46.567
Check this out,

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:48.333
a word analogy!

00:00:48.333 --> 00:00:50.700
Chicken is to egg,

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.067
as cow is to...

00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:53.667
what?

00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:54.267
A.

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:54.833
Milk,

00:00:54.833 --> 00:00:55.433
B.

00:00:55.433 --> 00:00:56.033
Grass,

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:56.600
C.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:57.200
Calf,

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.400
or D.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:00:58.967
Farm?

00:00:58.967 --> 00:01:00.167
Five seconds!

00:01:05.933 --> 00:01:07.133
TIME'S UP!

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:08.233
It's...

00:01:08.233 --> 00:01:08.700
A,

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:09.133
milk!

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:11.400
A chicken gives us eggs,

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.100
so a cow gives us milk.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:17.233
It is the food each animal provides.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:19.733
Check this out,

00:01:19.733 --> 00:01:21.533
fill in the blank!

00:01:21.533 --> 00:01:24.233
The museum guide gave such a

00:01:24.233 --> 00:01:26.900
blank talk that nobody in the

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:29.167
group wanted it to end.

00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:29.600
A.

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:30.033
Boring,

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:30.500
B.

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:30.933
Quiet,

00:01:30.933 --> 00:01:31.400
C.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:31.833
Short,

00:01:31.833 --> 00:01:32.733
or D.

00:01:32.733 --> 00:01:33.200
Fascinating?

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:34.067
Five seconds!

00:01:39.867 --> 00:01:41.067
TIME'S UP!

00:01:41.733 --> 00:01:42.233
It's...

00:01:42.233 --> 00:01:42.700
D,

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:43.200
fascinating!

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.167
If nobody wanted the talk to

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:46.633
end,

00:01:46.633 --> 00:01:48.600
it was very interesting.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.567
Fascinating means so interesting

00:01:50.567 --> 00:01:52.533
you cannot look away.

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:54.100
So,

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.133
are you smart or fart?

00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:58.567
Count up your correct answers to

00:01:58.567 --> 00:01:59.767
find your rank!

00:02:00.933 --> 00:02:01.267
So,

00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:02.667
how did you do?

00:02:02.667 --> 00:02:04.033
Comment your score below,

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:05.400
and follow for more!
